WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.460
Ok people, it's time for The Rubin Report
Fan Show, Round 2.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:14.690
Our first fan show was shot back in May of
2016, which seems like a lifetime ago, and

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.119
we are beyond due for another.

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:21.790
If you missed it entirely, we conducted 20
interviews in one day with Rubin Report fans

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:26.310
from all over the world, talking with viewers
from the United States and United Kingdom

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.820
to Egypt and Jordan to Switzerland and Sweden.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.590
What mattered more than the diversity of their
geographic location or their color or their

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.989
religion was their diversity of thought.

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:43.379
We had selected these 20 fans out of over
1400 submissions, and I promise you, we read

00:00:43.379 --> 00:00:45.010
every single one.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:50.749
These fans wrote us incredibly passionate
essays about their life, their work, and their

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:51.749
countries.

00:00:51.749 --> 00:00:56.530
It was virtually impossible to pick the final
20, and I can honestly say I loved every interview

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:57.859
I did.

00:00:57.859 --> 00:01:02.690
It was an incredibly long day for us and my
brain was fried after, but it truly was one

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:06.580
of the most rewarding and validating experiences
of my life.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.689
So many people being willing to stand up and
be part of the battle of ideas is everything

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:14.150
I've tried to foster here with this show.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:17.740
To say it was a humbling experience is beyond
and understatement.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.960
Actually, it was the fan show which really
sparked the idea us taking the show fully

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.020
independent.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:29.770
Just this week we crossed the 100 million
view mark, and I can't think of a better way

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:34.520
to mark this milestone than talking to you,
the fans, directly.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.619
This thing is really taking off and it is
you all who are the rocket fuel.

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:44.729
So far our second Fan Show: rubinreport.com/fanshow,
will take you to a submission page.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:48.999
Tell us a bit about yourself, where your from,
your age, why you watch the show and anything

00:01:48.999 --> 00:01:50.979
else you think is relevant.

00:01:50.979 --> 00:01:54.929
Please though, try to keep your submissions
under 10 sentences!

00:01:54.929 --> 00:01:58.409
We really loved reading the submissions last
time, but we need to make sure we have the

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:00.159
time to read to them all.

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:04.219
Be smart and succinct, and that'll be your
best way of getting through to us.

00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:08.310
If you're one of the 20 fans selected for
an interview, you'll hear from the Rubin Report

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.320
team sometime in April.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.620
If you submitted for the last fan show but
weren't selected, please submit again so we're

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.990
sure to see you!

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:21.940
And if you live in a place where free speech
isn't so free, please let us know how we can

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.280
accomodate, and we'll see what we can do.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:29.570
By the way if you're a $25 and up member on
Patreon, you've got a Golden Ticket opportunity

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:30.920
to be on the show.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:37.300
2 of the fan show guests will be selected
from this Patreon pool -- we've got a separate

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:42.930
form for you to fill out over at patreon.com/rubinreport.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:47.010
So many of you have told me that what we've
done here for the past two years has helped

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:52.120
create conversation in a time when sharing
ideas is becoming increasingly rare.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:57.180
This is your chance to say what you think
and be seen and heard by people who feel the

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.870
same way.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:03.010
You're just one person but the ultimate minority
is the individual.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.230
And an individual with a good idea can change
the world.

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:10.820
Go to rubinreport.com/fanshow, or click the
link below, and hopefully I'll talk to you

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:10.880
soon!

